                <pb facs="0859" n="755" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg755"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">411.12/1482: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-06-28T15:00:00-04:00">June 28, 1932—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>93. Your 114, June 25, 11 a.m., paragraph 6. Colonel
                        Moreno may remain in Mexico City during negotiation for en bloc
                    settlement. You will be further advised by telegraph of details of
                    arrangement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
